# PROPOSAL — copy into a fork's .github/CODEOWNERS (or repo root / docs/) to demo.
# Not written into ../diffusers/ automatically.
#
# Purpose: the Decision Declaration Linkage check (decision-linkage.yml) only verifies
# a declaration EXISTS and cites something real -- it never judges whether the citation
# is the right one or the understanding is correct. That's still a human's job. This
# file routes each domain's declarations to someone with actual authority to judge them
# -- in the real customer scenario, whoever maintains the corresponding .ai/<file>.md.
#
# Combined with branch protection's "Require review from Code Owners", this is a second
# server-enforced (Tier 1) mechanism, purely additive -- a text file plus a checkbox,
# no new machinery to build or own.
#
# Two tradeoffs to say out loud, not hide:
#   1. Concentrating required approval on a small owner set can itself become a
#      bottleneck -- reviewer workload/participation are stronger drivers of review
#      timeliness than most other factors in the literature (Kononenko/McIntosh). This
#      trades "no gate" for "a gate that can queue on one person." Widen the owner
#      groups (teams, not individuals) if this becomes the new bottleneck.
#   2. On a solo fork there is no second human to demo a genuine catch with this file --
#      the live demo shows the CODEOWNERS wiring itself, not a real second-reviewer
#      moment. Say this rather than imply the demo proves more than it does.

# Domain                              Owner (placeholder — real maintainers of the
#                                      corresponding .ai/<file>.md in the actual repo)
src/diffusers/models/                 @models-domain-owners
src/diffusers/pipelines/              @pipelines-domain-owners
src/diffusers/schedulers/             @pipelines-domain-owners
src/diffusers/guiders/                @pipelines-domain-owners
src/diffusers/modular_pipelines/      @modular-domain-owners
